            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0637" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg544"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1631/111: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in El Salvador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-01T12:00:00-04:00">May 1, 1935—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. Your despatch 213, April 13. In view of the probability that loan
                    negotiations will be protracted, the Department prefers, unless you perceive
                    strong objections, that you submit Schedule I without further delay.</p>
                <p>It is hoped that an agreement can be reached in time for presentation to the
                    present Congress in El Salvador.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
